<title>FRANCE: French sugar consumption declined in November - FIRS.</title>
<headline>French sugar consumption declined in November - FIRS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>French sugar consumption dropped to a provisonal 163,000 tonnes in November from a revised 196,000 tonnes in October, French sugar intervention board FIRS said.</p>
<p>But consumption rose from 144,700 tonnes in November 1995, FIRS said in its January report.</p>
<p>This would bring cumulative sales to the French market for the first two months of the 1996/97 season (Oct-Sept) to 359,000 tonnes against 311,724 tonnes in the same period for 1995/96.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
